*Lines 57–69.* Explodes the `item_codes` list column into a long `(student_number, item_code, count)` table. Skips rows where `item_codes` is not a non-empty `list`, and skips falsy codes. Returns an empty DataFrame **with** columns `["student_number","item_code","count"]` when there is nothing to count.

> **This definition is dead.** A second `def _itemCodeCounts(df)` at line 2385 rebinds the name at import time, so every caller resolves to the later version (§5.7).

