*Lines 72–77.* Returns `{lvl: pct}` — the percentage of non-null values equal to each level, rounded to 1 dp; all-NaN input returns `{lvl: np.nan}`.

> **Unused.** `getFlagDf` defines its own nested `_lvl_dist` (line 2181) which returns `0.0` rather than `np.nan` for empty input.

#### `_buildCountPivot(cohortDf, formType, mappingFile=None)`

*Lines 80–118.* Student × item_code (Simulation) or student × Section (Clinic) **count** pivot.

**Parameters**

| Name | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `cohortDf` | `DataFrame` | — | Form-level rows with `item_codes`, `student_number`, `student_name` |
| `formType` | `str` | — | `"Clinic"` triggers section mapping; anything else groups by raw item code |
